---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is built.">
  <div class="column">
    <h1 class="page-title">Colophon</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The design borrows from Football Manager's player profile screens: attributes out of 20, a form guide, a
        scout report. The skins follow the time of day, night to dawn to day, unless you pick one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, set in Archivo, hosted on Cloudflare. Content is plain
        Markdown in a git repo, and the source is on <a href="https://github.com/jsphelps12/PersonalSite">GitHub</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Posts go up through an MCP server, so I can write by talking to Claude. More on that in the <a href="/projects/personal-site">project writeup</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Coming eventually: a JoshGPT that's actually an AI.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .column {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
</style>
